    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Taylor Ward** (71.18) and **Bryson Stott** (70.43) headline our offensive output, anchored by favorable matchups against Erick Fedde and Bubba Chandler, respectively. **Taylor Ward** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Fedde (5.20 xERA) and the favorable hitting environment, which, combined with his premium spot in the #2 hole, provides an elite ceiling. Similarly, **Bryson Stott** finds himself in a high-leverage spot; the combination of a strong wind-out projection (+5%) and an advantageous matchup against Chandler allows him to outperform his base projection. **Tyler Freeman** (70.09) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.51) also register as strong plays, with **Tyler Freeman** particularly interesting due to his speed profile and the added +2% efficiency bump from the opponent's slow delivery, which maximizes his potential to secure those highly-coveted stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Daulton Varsho** (49.36), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Daulton Varsho** held a solid platoon advantage against Nolan McLean, his score was dragged down by the high-skill profile of the opposing pitcher (3.28 xERA) and his middle-of-the-order placement. The optimizer preferred the higher individual upside and park-factor boosts found in our starting outfielders. We are proceeding with caution regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, including **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz**; should the official lineups shift these players into lower-priority slots or result in a benching, we will lose significant efficiency. Furthermore, we continue to monitor the IL status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains unavailable, leaving us to rely on our active core to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 race.",
